# The driver is built and published by its own repository now; this file only pins a
# release. See docs/development/panvk-mali-g77-bringup.md section 31.
PANVK_REPO=ryanistr/PanVK-rynx
PANVK_TAG=PanVK-rynx-1.2.0-p8
PANVK_SHA256=5b659e75629c94d2ea22b73d135a795a8c08b799859046b1d6012c201314ea81
# Built from the Mali-G57 fork (now ryanistr/PanVK-rynx, build.sh + its patches) rather than from
# our own mesa-patches: only that tree has a Valhall JM backend at all, and from v1.2.0 it gates the
# external memory/semaphore fd group on PANVK_FD_INTEROP, which gamescope requires. p13 shipped no
# v9 backend, so a Valhall device enumerated no GPU and gamescope reported no physical device.
# p4 additionally carries 0003, which ports Valhall gen3 (arch 11, Mali-G615/G715) back into the
# fork; without it a GT 30 Pro has the same "no physical device" failure as p13 had on a G77.
#
# The driver names itself after its tag from p5 on: PanVK-rynx-<version>-<patch>, e.g.
# PanVK-rynx-1.2.0-p5. That code name is what tells this fork's build apart from any other PanVK
# package in the driver lists, the device report and a bug report; it is written by the build
# script and read back by LinuxPanvkDriverManager.getBuiltinName(). Since the p1-p6 retag it is
# also the release tag and title and the asset's own name: every earlier patch shipped the same
# file name, panvk-linux-g57-1.2.0.tzst, and PanvkReleases records a download by asset name, so
# the list could never offer a newer patch of the same line.
#
# p7 is the published one: p6 plus 0009 (the Mali-G77 model row) and 0010 (the real swapchain
# BO dump). p6 added the CSF fixes to p4: 0004 (the CSF provoking-vertex address
# truncation), 0005 (kbase reports node rdev as a DRM device), 0006 (single merged CSG with
# fence-wait reclaim) and 0007 (the CS register file sized from the kbase uAPI instead of a fixed 96,
# plus the missing nr_kernel_registers on the job-emission builder; that pair is
# wonderkast02/panvk-g720-kbase-csf 0.1.0-beta.2's fix, arrived at from the other end) and 0008
# (advertise VK_EXT_physical_device_drm when those numbers are known - without it 0005 fills two
# fields nothing can read, which is what a p5 session measured; bringup §22). It declares gpuArch
# [9, 10, 11]. To publish the next one:
#   gh workflow run release.yml -R ryanistr/PanVK-rynx -f version=1.2.0 -f tag=PanVK-rynx-1.2.0-p<n>
# then set PANVK_TAG/PANVK_SHA256 here to the new asset and re-run tools/build_local.sh.
# The release must exist in PANVK_REPO before a build can fetch it; the p7 bytes are the
# same asset that used to live in ryanistr/DroidDeck-Mali, so re-upload them under this tag.
PANVK_SOURCE="PanVK-rynx (ryanistr/PanVK-rynx), from mesa-panvk-mali-g57 v1.2.0"
PANVK_WORKFLOW=ryanistr/PanVK-rynx/.github/workflows/release.yml
